# Normalize every text file to LF in the index and in the working tree on all
# platforms. This is load-bearing for CI: the `git diff --exit-code` step in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml must be a byte comparison, and the GitHub Windows
# runner sets core.autocrlf=true globally.
#
#   text=auto (index side)    -- keeps a CRLF blob from ever being committed. A
#                                CRLF entry in the index would false-positive
#                                that diff step on every Windows run, forever.
#   eol=lf    (worktree side) -- overrides core.autocrlf so gofmt's LF output
#                                matches what was checked out, instead of
#                                rewriting every .go file on each Windows run.
#
# Safe to introduce here: `git ls-files --eol` reports i/lf for every tracked
# text file, so `git add --renormalize .` is a no-op and no existing checkout
# sees a one-time renormalization diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The only tracked binary. text=auto would already exclude it via git's NUL-byte
# heuristic; stating it explicitly removes that dependency.
*.png binary
